  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x201c;Local First: transforming the peacebuilding system&#x201d;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme is one of nine programmes under the Contributing to Peaceful and Safe Societies 2024-2031 (CPSS) grant policy framework by Peace Direct.Peace Direct was established in 2004 and partners directly with local civil society organisations in 14 countries, with over 20 partners. It is Peace Direct&#x2019;s core belief that the potential and agency of local people can bring about change and build peace.The &#x201c;Local First: transforming the peacebuilding system&#x201d; programme aims to bridge the gap between policy makers and power holders on the one side; and locally led peacebuilding actors on the other side.The strategic objective of the programme is: &#x201c;local peacebuilding efforts in the four targeted countries, and internationally, will be better resources, acknowledged and supported by the international community, leading to increased prospects for sustainable peace&#x201d;.</narrative>
  </description>
